            <ArticleTitle>Factors Associated with Delayed Presentation and Misdiagnosis of Testicular Torsion: A Case-Control Study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>200-204</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3476(17)30386-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2017.03.037</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We identified factors associated with delay in presentation and misdiagnosis of testicular torsion. Compared with acute cases, delayed presentations were more likely to report isolated abdominal pain, developmental disorders, and history of recent genital trauma. Failure to perform a genitourinary examination or scrotal imaging was associated with misdiagnosis.</AbstractText>
